  "techniqueFacts": [
    "all four sources blend their own dry spices into the browned mince — no packet chilli spice-mix sachet appears in any source (a GF risk avoided)",
    "s2 tags the dish gluten free and names beef stock as the only GF swap point ('gluten-free if required'); s0 also categorises the recipe gluten-free",
    "s2 gives a homemade chilli spice mix: 2 tsp smoked paprika, 2 tsp dried oregano, 2 tsp onion powder, 1 tsp cumin, 1 tsp ground coriander",
    "covered low simmer 30-45 min is universal; s0 instead bakes covered at 180 C for 45 min",
    "spices are cooked into the meat before liquids in all sources (bloomed, not stirred in at the end)",
    "flavour improves after a day or two in the fridge (2 sources); freezes up to 3 months (3 sources)",
    "s1 is a beanless Tex-Mex outlier: ketchup, American mustard, allspice, cider vinegar, no tomatoes or beans",
    "s3 doubles the beans (kidney + black) for a big batch; chipotle sauce is its optional heat source",
    "s2 finishes by grilling grated cheese on top of the pan"
